    pr_ref:  # 6a8d
    description: "## Origin\n\nSplit from **WI-harin** (io-boundary db_* gap) during clean-scope execution\n(owner-ratified \"clean-scope + refile\", 2026-07-16). WI-harin populated the\nPython stdlib db_* catalog (sqlite3/dbm/shelve) and fixed the\nexecute_from_command_line net_recv FP (PR #685, dev a58b18f82a), but the\nDOMINANT symptom in WI-harin's body — third-party ORM I/O invisible, driving\nio_tag_rate to ~0.5% on Django repos — is NOT a catalog problem and is\ntransferred here.\n\n## Symptom (io-security data-loss; P1-severity impact, receiver-inference fix)\n\nOn framework-heavy Python repos the io-boundary detector sees almost no I/O\nbecause the real I/O is third-party ORM/cache/client calls. On pretix\n(Django/Celery, DEEP cohort deep-20260623-134237 iter-004): total_io_edges =\n191/101342 (0.19%), io_tag_rate ~0.5%. The bulk is Django ORM —\nmeasured against pretix's live survey (hg.json):\n\n| Callee (short) | calls | is_resolved=false |\n|---|---|---|\n| save   | 1841 | 1689 (92%) |\n| get    | 1863 | 1615 (87%) |\n| delete | 206  | 173 |\n| filter | 205  | 189 |\n| update | 156  | 118 |\n| atomic | 100  | 100 |\n| execute (cursor) | 16 | 15 |\n\nAll arrive as **bare untyped unresolved external method calls**: dst =\n`python:external:0-0:<name>:external_symbol`, `is_resolved=false`,\n`call_construct=\"method\"`, **no module hint**.\n\n## Why the catalog can't reach this (verified — do NOT re-attempt catalog entries)\n\nThe io-boundary matcher (io_boundary.py `lookup_with_module` ->\n`gate_named_entry`) CORRECTLY refuses these: with `call_construct=\"method\"`\nand no module hint, `gate_named_entry` returns None (INV-tapat/INV-maluk — an\nuntyped method call cannot be verified against a catalogued receiver type;\nthe same guard that stops bare `.replace()` matching `pathlib.Path.replace`).\nCataloging `save`/`get`/`filter`/`all` by short name would either match\nnothing (suppressed) or explode into false positives — `get` alone is 1863\nhits, dominated by `dict.get`/`cache.get`, not ORM. This is a hard invariant,\nnot a bug to work around.\n\n## Fix: receiver-type inference for external-base method dispatch\n\nMake ORM db_* visible by TYPING the receiver, then let the existing catalog +\nmodule-filter path classify it:\n\n- **Django ORM writes:** `self.save()` / `self.delete()` where the enclosing\n  class subclasses `django.db.models.Model` (external base, trackable via the\n  `extends` edge to the external Model) -> db_write. Model instances passed\n  around similarly.\n- **Django ORM reads:** `<Model>.objects.filter()/get()/all()/count()` — the\n  `objects` attribute is a Manager; type `<Model>.objects` -> Manager ->\n  db_read on its query methods.\n- **`transaction.atomic`:** dotted `django.db.transaction.atomic` already\n  carries the `django.db` module segment — a targeted qualified-name catalog\n  entry could catch this subset without inference (small, separable).\n- **SQLAlchemy:** `Session.query/execute/add/commit`, `Engine.execute` — same\n  external-base receiver typing.\n- **Raw DBAPI:** `cursor.execute` / `conn.execute` — type `conn =\n  sqlite3.connect(...)` / `cur = conn.cursor()` receivers (mirrors the WI-fuvuj\n  `file` synthetic-module trick), which also activates the LATENT db_* method\n  entries WI-harin already catalogued (sqlite3.Cursor.execute, fetch*, ...).\n\n## Approach options (design fork — checkpoint before building)\n\n1. **Django-specific heuristic:** detect `models.Model`-subclass receivers +\n   a Manager (`objects`) heuristic. Bounded, high pretix payoff, per-framework\n   maintenance.\n2. **General external-base receiver inference:** resolve method dispatch on a\n   receiver whose declared/inferred type has an external base, and consult a\n   framework-role map. Broader (SQLAlchemy, requests-session, redis client),\n   more work, touches py.py resolution internals (dispatch:F3 / WI-noham\n   family — dominant risk is over-suppression breaking the ~15 dispatch:F3\n   receiver-resolution tests, which must be re-run).\n\n## Family (siblings, NOT duplicates)\n\n- **WI-fabup** — wire `ambiguous_names` to receiver disambiguation for\n  RESOLVED receivers (get/patch/run). Complementary: assumes the receiver\n  type is known; this item is about receivers with NO type (unresolved\n  external), needing inference from the external base.\n- **WI-fuvuj** (done) — the `file` synthetic-module receiver-type trick for\n  `open()` results. The precedent pattern to extend to sqlite3/ORM receivers.\n- **INV-fahub** — receiver-blind resolution umbrella (bakeoff-gated).\n\n## Repro\n\n`hypergumbo io-boundaries` on a Django repo (pretix in /tmp/f5_cohort_pool or\nthe DEEP artifact out/cohort-001/iter-004/pretix/) -> total_io_edges near-zero\ndespite heavy ORM use; io_tag_rate ~0.5%."  # 6a8d
