  nonce: '6853'  # 6853
  message: "Done (Django increment) in PR #695 (dev 5dcfad4927). SHIPPED: type-verified receiver typing for Django ORM db I/O — py.py emits django.db.models module-qualified calls edges for (a) the <Model>.objects.<method>() Manager marker (chained receiver previously emitted NO edge) and (b) models.Model-subclass self.save()/self.delete() (re-keyed additively, without touching the guarded INV-fahub/WI-noham receiver-hint chain); a python.yaml type-verified carve-out classifies them db_read/db_write via the module-filter path — never the short-name gate, so no dict.get()/.save() FP (INV-tapat/INV-maluk preserved); db_write->database-sink / db_read->untrusted-source taint wiring free.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (re-ran the filed pretix repro on the production path analyze_python -> tag_io_boundaries over /tmp/f5_cohort_pool/pretix/src): 4677 Django ORM db edges now tagged (2251 db_read + 2426 db_write; top methods create 2343, filter 1125, get 653, count 105) where the FILED repro measured total_io_edges=191 with the ORM entirely INVISIBLE. Every ORM-operation edge classifies; the other ~2606 django.db.models edges are pre-existing models.Q/F/Sum/field-type instantiations (query-expression builders) correctly NOT tagged. ~47% of tagged edges have test-file src. Plus 21 co-located unit/integration tests (14 producer + 7 catalog), 100% coverage in isolation.\n\nApproach + catalog-home forks decided WITH OWNER over a 5-agent ADR/spec/spirit investigation: Django-specific type-verified .objects. marker over general external-base inference (which would touch the ~110-test dispatch:F3 internals — the INV-junid-declined general-mechanism shape); python.yaml carve-out over a framework-scoped catalog (WI-harin's exclusion was a PRECISION rule vs short-name matching, which a type-verified real-module entry dissolves — the catalog already carries flask.Flask.run/javax.persistence).\n\nDEFERRED to residual WI-sitos-lavoj-kigis-padup-lufiz-fovuv-piloh-vakur: SQLAlchemy Session.*, instance.save() on a typed local (return-type inference — the ~25% <localvar>.M() write recall), transitive Model bases. Tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation (io_tag_rate improvement claim)."  # 6853
