  message: "BAKEOFF-VALIDATED — directed DEEP io_tag_rate validation on the Django cohort (pretix), 2026-07-16. Reproduced the bakeoff metric (total_io_edges/calls_total*100) faithfully: full 'hypergumbo survey' (9m12s) + 'io-boundaries' on pretix at current dev, vs the recorded iter-005 baseline of session deep-20260623-134237.\n\n  BEFORE (iter-005, pre-WI-sozoj): io_tag_rate 0.50%, total_io_edges 187, database chains 0, calls_total 37598 — reproduces the recorded 0.5% LOW_IO_TAG_RATE warning EXACTLY (clean baseline).\n  AFTER  (current dev, WI-sozoj): io_tag_rate 2.56%, total_io_edges 1033, database chains 846 (db_read 736 + db_write 110), calls_total 40429.\n\nRESULT: io_tag_rate 0.50% -> 2.56% (5.1x), clearing the size-scaled LOW_IO_TAG_RATE threshold (0.80% at pretix's 36603 nodes) by 3.2x — WARN -> PASS. Database boundary 0 -> 846 chains; EVERY other boundary byte-identical (env_read 62, logging 51, fs_read 46, fs_write 14, subprocess 4, net_send 2, browser_storage 8) — pure gain, no regression. MOVED -> awaits_bakeoff_validation tag stripped."  # db68
